 appeared only in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with user/timestamp fields, while the auth.log COMMAND= count stayed frozen at 6 (only unrelated PAM session open/close lines continued there)","Captured pre-restart baseline boot IDs and health on node1 and node2","Restarted node1 via sudo systemctl reboot (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect), polled until reachable, confirmed new boot ID and that the sudoers drop-in, log file, and logging behavior (no new auth.log COMMAND= entries) survived the reboot","Restarted node2 via sudo systemctl reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot ID and systemctl is-system-running=running plus working sudo"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Sudo commands are recorded with user and timestamp to /var/log/sudo-commands.log","command_ids":["cmd-9f47374e33b7486e","cmd-e952228406214520","cmd-7f39b240cbce4107"],"summary":"Playbook run created the sudoers drop-in; subsequent sudo commands (id -u, systemctl is-active, tail, etc.) appear in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with format 'Mon DD HH:MM:SS YYYY : user : PWD=... ; USER=... ; COMMAND=...'"},{"requirement":"Entries are kept out of the general system log","command_ids":["cmd-e952228406214520","cmd-9ad0c64d36dc4ac4","cmd-7f39b240cbce4107"],"summary":"auth.log had exactly 6 COMMAND= entries from pre-change baseline sudo calls (apt-get, tee, whoami, grep); after applying the sudoers !syslog directive, additional sudo commands (ls, systemctl, wc, grep, tail) did not add any new COMMAND= lines to auth.log — count stayed at 6 across multiple subsequent commands"},{"requirement":"Implemented using Ansible","command_ids":["cmd-ff36a126b27f4a9b","cmd-727793a8cc6b4ff6","cmd-d3c1a4b0a16b437c","cmd-9f47374e33b7486e"],"summary":"Ansible installed via apt; playbook.yml authored with file and sudoers copy(validate=visudo) tasks; ansible-playbook run against localhost with connection=local completed changed=2/failed=0"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement